    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Castlemoyne is an attractive Shannon Homes development, built circa 2006. No. 138 enjoys a prime position just off the Malahide Road, adjacent to protected natural green areas offering plenty of open space in a safe settled environment. This highly sought-after and well-established development provides well maintained parks, landscaped greens, and a dedicated children’s playground, making it ideal for families.\r\n\r\nThe nearby coastal villages of Portmarnock, Malahide, Baldoyle, Sutton and Howth offer an exceptional lifestyle, with scenic coastal walks, renowned restaurants, bars, yacht clubs, golf courses, as well as a range of churches and schools. Public transport is well catered for, with DART and regular bus services providing easy access to the city centre and there is an excellent selection of shops 7 restaurants nearby at Balgriffin, within a short walk from home. There are two primary schools within walking distance, while the M50, M1, and Dublin Airport are all within a 15-minute drive.\r\n\r\nNo 138 comprises an attractive red brick semi-detached family home, presented in exceptionally good order. The accommodation extends to c.1,527 square feet with an additional c.375 square feet of attic space. The accommodation briefly comprises a reception hall with a wc & whb, understairs storage, a living room to the front with a fireplace, double doors lead into an impressive extended space at the rear with extra high ceilings filling the kitchen, dining, and living space with plenty of natural sun light. The kitchen offers a range of painted wall and floor mounted cabinetry with integrated appliances and a separate utility space for added convenience.\r\n \r\nAt first floor level, there are four well-proportioned bedrooms, one of which benefits from an en-suite, along with a main family bathroom. The second floor comprises a superb and spacious main bedroom, featuring a second en-suite.\r\n \r\nThe central heating is gas fired and the energy rating is a healthy B2 confirming this energy efficient home has so much to offer its fortunate new owners. \r\n\r\nViewing is available by appointment with Gallagher Quigley; all enquiries are welcome to info@gallagherquigley.ie"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 5.62m x 1.94m \r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room - 6.61m x 3.95m \r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room - 7.46m x 5.99m \r\n\r\n\r\nUtility Room - 1.58m x 1.35m \r\n\r\n\r\nWC - 1.84m x 1.18m \r\n\r\n\r\nLanding - 2.0m x 2.82m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 4.52m x 3.07m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.87m x 2.89m \r\n\r\n\r\nEn-suite - 1.65m x 2.26m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 2.65m x 2.82m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 - 2.45m x 2.82m \r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom - 2.35m x 1.81m \r\n\r\n\r\nHot press - \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 5 - 5.62m x 3.62m \r\n\r\n\r\nShower Room - 1.74m x 2.26m \r\n\r\n\r\nStore - 1.75m x 2.26m \r\n\r\n\r\n"
